%% Trace: FR-11–FR-15, FR-19, FR-47–FR-48, FR-61; UC-07/08; SC-05/06
%% Scope: Three separate state domains: a version, a search job, and document availability. No combined product Draft state.
%% Legend: Revision creates a NEW Current identity; the old instance becomes Superseded. Guards, expected revision, idempotency and local audit are prerequisites, not shown as lifecycle states.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "Version: Current" as Current
    state "Version: Superseded<br/>Immutable historical bytes" as Superseded
    state "Version: Archived<br/>Only explicit history if readable" as Archived
    state "Job: pending<br/>New attempt uses a fresh job/generation" as Pending
    state "Job: ready<br/>Exact version/revision/generation match" as Ready
    state "Job: failed<br/>Semantic unavailable; keyword independent" as Failed
    state "Document: available<br/>Current pointer may be null after archive" as Available
    state "Document: unavailable<br/>Monotonic logical deletion; no revival<br/>Physical purge/retention undecided" as Unavailable
    Current --> Superseded: revise: same transaction installs a NEW Current
    Current --> Archived: archive Current; clear current pointer
    Superseded --> Archived: archive historical version
    Pending --> Ready: matching job succeeds
    Pending --> Failed: processing fails
    Failed --> Pending: retry same job identity while still valid
    Available --> Unavailable: authorised delete; invalidate jobs and protected reads
